  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city's old town is a maze of narrow streets and historic buildings. It was once the centre of trade for the entire region, but now it's largely touristy. Visitors come from all over to see the famous cathedral, which dates back to the 12th century. Some people complain that the area has become too commercialized, while others argue that the influx of tourists is bringing in much-needed revenue.\n\nDespite its popularity, the old town still retains some of its original charm. The streets are lined with quaint shops and restaurants, and there's a lively atmosphere on weekends when locals come out to socialize. However, it's worth noting that the area can get quite crowded during peak season, making it difficult for residents to navigate.\n\nIn recent years, efforts have been made to preserve the old town's heritage while also accommodating the needs of tourists. This has included the restoration of historic buildings and the creation of new public spaces. While some critics argue that these changes are eroding the area's authenticity, others see them as a necessary step towards ensuring its long-term viability.\n\nAs one local resident put it, 'The old town is a treasure trove of history and culture, but we need to be mindful of how we preserve it for future generations.'\"\n\n---\n\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The city's old town has become too commercialized.\", \"Tourism is bringing in much-needed revenue.\", \"The area is being preserved for future generations.\", \"The streets are lined with quaint shops and restaurants.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The city's old town has become too commercialized.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the cathedral in the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It was destroyed during a war.\", \"It dates back to the 12th century.\", \"It's no longer open to visitors.\", \"It's located outside the old town.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It dates back to the 12th century.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards the preservation of the old town?\",\n      \"options\": [\"He thinks it should be left untouched.\", \"He believes it's a necessary step towards ensuring its long-term viability.\", \"He's indifferent to the issue.\", \"He thinks it's eroding the area's authenticity.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"He believes it's a necessary step towards ensuring its long-term viability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the local resident who was quoted in the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They're opposed to tourism.\", \"They think the old town is being preserved for future generations.\", \"They're concerned about the area's authenticity.\", \"They're a long-time resident of the city.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"They're concerned about the area's authenticity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the purpose of the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To persuade readers to visit the old town.\", \"To inform readers about the history of the cathedral.\", \"To discuss the pros and cons of tourism in the area.\", \"To describe the efforts being made to preserve the old town's heritage.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To describe the efforts being made to preserve the old town's heritage.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
